# Copy the appropriate block into the corresponding .env file.
# None of the .env* files (except this one) are tracked by git.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env  —  Developer read-only Basic Auth key
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source: Ravelry developer portal > App settings > "basic_auth_username" / "basic_auth_password"
# Scope:  Public catalog endpoints only.  Cannot call authenticated endpoints.
#         Use for pattern/yarn search, shop lookup, reference data, etc.
#
# RAVELRY_USERNAME=read-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# RAVELRY_API_KEY=your_basic_auth_password
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.user.read  —  User personal read key
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source: Ravelry developer portal > App settings > "access_key" / "personal_key"
# Scope:  Full read access to your Ravelry account.  All OAuth scopes granted
#         automatically — no explicit scope list needed.
#         Use for stash, projects, queue, favorites, messages, needles, library, etc.
#
# RAVELRY_USERNAME=your_access_key
# RAVELRY_API_KEY=your_personal_key
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.user.readwrite  —  User personal read/write key
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source: Same portal credentials as .env.user.read (personal key grants both read and write).
# Scope:  Full read AND write access.  Use for scripts that mutate data:
#         creating/updating projects, posting to forums, sending messages, etc.
#         Write operations require forum-write / message-write scopes — both are
#         granted automatically with the personal key.
#
# RAVELRY_USERNAME=your_access_key
# RAVELRY_API_KEY=your_personal_key
